</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.5.2 </span>Learnt Weight of Shared Matrix</h4>

<div id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We visualize the learned knocking-heads projection parameters in Fig. <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 4.5.2 Learnt Weight of Shared Matrix ‣ 4.5 Visualization ‣ 4 Experiment ‣ Knocking-Heads Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, both applied before QK normalization, show similar block-structured patterns: some feature dimensions exhibit low diagonal values indicating inter-head interaction learning, while others retain high diagonal values for head-specific information. Some layers even exhibit minimal inter-head interaction, highlighting the adaptive nature of our method. Notably, <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{V}</annotation></semantics></math> displays a distinct pattern with consistently low diagonal values across layers, indicating aggressive head-sharing. This may explain why value projections yield greater improvements in Table. <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2.1 KHA with Varying Head Number ‣ 4.2 Architecture Exploration On Attention ‣ 4 Experiment ‣ Knocking-Heads Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. When using MLPs, the gate matrices also exhibit clear structural patterns.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
